Micky Cross.text:
{{short description|Irish hurler (1902–1977)}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=December 2021}}

'''Michael Cross''' (4 March 1902 – 17 July 1977) was an Irish [[hurling|hurler]] who played as a right wing-back and as a left corner-back for the [[Limerick GAA|Limerick]] senior team.<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.askaboutireland.ie/aai-files/assets/libraries/limerick-city-library/reading-room/sport/micky-cross.pdf|title=Great Limerick Athletes: No 147 – Micky Cross of Claughaun|publisher=Limerick website|access-date=4 October 2011}}</ref>

Cross made his first appearance for the team during the [[All-Ireland Senior Hurling Championship 1923|1923 championship]] and became a regular player over the next decade-and-a-half. During that time he won two [[All-Ireland Senior Hurling Championship|All-Ireland]] winner's medals, five [[Munster Senior Hurling Championship|Munster]] winner's medals and four [[National Hurling League]] winners' medals.<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.hoganstand.com/limerick/Profile.aspx|title=County profile: Limerick|publisher=Hogan Stand website|access-date=4 October 2011|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120525185227/http://www.hoganstand.com/Limerick/Profile.aspx|archive-date=25 May 2012}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|url=http://munster.gaa.ie/history/sh_teams/|title=Munster Senior Hurling|publisher=Munster GAA website|access-date=4 October 2011|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190328073637/http://munster.gaa.ie/history/sh_teams/|archive-date=28 March 2019|url-status=dead}}</ref>

At club level, Cross played with [[Claughaun GAA|Claughaun]] and won two [[Limerick Senior Hurling Championship|county championship]] winners' medals in a career that spanned three decades.{{citation needed|date=December 2021}}

Gleeson also won four [[Railway Cup]] winners' medal when he was picked for the [[Munster GAA|Munster]] inter-provincial teams and also represented Ireland in the [[Tailteann Games (Irish Free State)|Tailteann Games]].{{citation needed|date=December 2021}}

