Ger Cunningham (Limerick hurler).text:
{{short description|Irish hurler}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=January 2022}}
{{Use Irish English|date=January 2022}}
'''Ger Cunningham''' (born 1972) is an [[Irish people|Irish]] retired [[hurling|hurler]] who played for the [[Limerick GAA|Limerick]] minor team.

Born in [[Knockainey]], [[County Limerick]], Cunningham first arrived on the inter-county scene at the age of seventeen when he first linked up with the Limerick minor team. At club level, Cunningham played with [[Knockainey GAA|Knockainey Hurling Club]].{{fact|date=January 2022}}

In retirement from playing Cunningham became involved in team management and coaching. At club level he was an [[All-Ireland Senior Club Hurling Championship|All-Ireland]]-winning coach with [[Newtownshandrum GAA|Newtownshandrum]] before steering [[Thurles Sarsfields GAA|Thurles Sarsfields]] to a first [[Tipperary Senior Hurling Championship|championship]] in over thirty years.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.independent.ie/sport/hurling/cork-club-find-a-new-ger-cunningham-26016260.html|title=Cork club find a new Ger Cunningham|publisher=Irish Independent|date=12 February 2004|accessdate=28 May 2015|first=Colm|last=Keys}}</ref> Cunningham has served as a selector with the Limerick minor and senior teams, before becoming technical coach with the Laois senior team. On 28 May 2015 he was appointed interim manager of the Laois senior team.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.limerickleader.ie/sport/limerick-sport/limerick-s-cunningham-appointed-laois-hurling-manager-1-6767561|title=Limerick’s Cunningham appointed Laois hurling manager|publisher=Limerick Leader|date=28 May 2015|accessdate=28 May 2015|first=|last=}}</ref>

